The first constructor comparison exposed a syntax-layer distinction, not a program difference: K claims spell empty list units as `.Exprs`/`.Stmts`, while standalone `.mpy` syntax represents those units by omission. I’m applying only that explicit unit normalization and rerunning the parser-level comparison; the ground claim already closed, and the material body mutation produced the expected stuck residual (`D ≠ 99`).
